\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Clone-generation results on the industrial measurement and control corpus. Twelve programs $\times $ three seeds $=$ 36 runs per configuration. \emph  {Equiv.\ conf.} is reported over categories C and D only --- six subjects, 18 runs per configuration --- these being the programs that ship golden vectors and invariants; categories A and B have no equivalence probes and are excluded rather than scored as passes.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:results}{{1}{5}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Blind LLM review of all 108 generated clones. An independent model (\texttt  {claude-opus-5}, distinct from the \texttt  {claude-sonnet-5} used for generation) was shown each original and its clone with all system-identifying markers removed, and asked for concrete behavioural defects. \textsc  {no-op} denotes a clone byte-identical to its original: trivially faithful because nothing was attempted, and therefore excluded from the clean rate rather than counted as a success.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:judge}{{2}{5}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Precision of each configuration's own success signal. Of the clones a configuration certified (compiles, passes the full suite, and genuinely substituted the dependency), the fraction an independent blind reviewer found to carry \textsc  {broken} or \textsc  {major} behavioural defects. Accepting more clones and accepting sound clones are different capabilities, and they trade off against one another.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:precision}{{3}{6}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces test}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:results}{{1}{6}}
